8. In Smt. Nagawwa vs. Veeranna Shivallngappa Konjalgi, AIR 1976 (SC) 1947,
Hon'ble Apex Court held that an order of the Magistrate issuing process against the accused can be quashed or set aside only in following cases:
(A) Where the allegations made in the complaint, or the statements of the witnesses recorded in support of the same taken at their face value make out absolutely no case against the accused or the complaint does not disclose the essential SUBHASH ingredients of an offence which is alleged against the accused;
